It may be physically impossible to quantify how much any given program or intervention has improved safety.

But one thing we're fairly confident in is that aviation safety has improved since, say, the 70's or 80's. We've measured the fatal accident rate, in both relative and absolute terms, almost obsessively.

The only problem is, no one can say for certain WHY safety has improved. Was it the improvement in the design and technology of airliners? Was it a result of the safety programs implemented as a collaborative effort by the government and industry? Some combination of the two? This is the problem. It is difficult to pin it down with any certainty.